jobs.description:
As an Industrial Cleaning Specialist, your primary responsibility is to clean and prepare returned packaging materials for reuse. This includes removing stickers, barcodes, and labels, as well as occasionally disassembling and reassembling products. The job is both physically active and varied, offering you new challenges every day. If you thrive on being hands-on and enjoy an active role, this is the perfect opportunity for you.

Your key tasks include:

- Cleaning formwork and other packaging materials;
- Removing stickers, barcodes, and labels without damaging surfaces;
- Disassembling and reassembling products as needed.

You’ll work in two shifts: early (06:00–15:00) and late (15:00–00:00), ensuring flexibility and variety in your schedule.

- Proficiency in English;
- Physical fitness and ability to perform active work throughout the day;
- Availability for two-shift work without exceptions.

This is not your average production environment. The organisation you'll be joining is a global frontrunner in identity security, think biometric passports, secure payment cards, facial recognition at international airports, and cryptographic systems used by governments and banks worldwide. 

As Maintenance Engineer, you are the backbone of a smooth-running production floor. When machines go down, you're the one who gets things moving again, but more importantly, you make sure they don't go down in the first place. You combine hands-on technical skill with a structured mindset: you don't just fix problems, you prevent them. 

What you'll be doing

- Keeping production equipment in top condition and reducing unplanned downtime;
- Building and executing preventive maintenance schedules;
- Digging into the root cause of breakdowns — not just patching things up;
- Translating technical findings into clear documentation and practical improvement plans;
- Supporting the roll-out and commissioning of new equipment;
- Working with software controls for production machinery;
- Collaborating with production, management, and other departments on both day-to-day operations and longer-term reliability improvements;
- Monitoring facility and utility systems to ensure a safe working environment.

- An MBO level 4 background in Electrical or Manufacturing Engineering (or equivalent experience);
- A proven track record in a maintenance role within a production environment;
- Good command of English, spoken and written;
- Flexibility to work in shifts and join an on-call rotation;
- Willingness to occasionally travel for training or visits to other sites;
- Strong communication skills and a collaborative attitude.

Do you already have some experience in purchasing, supply chain, or logistics and are you ready for the next step in your career? Would you like to work in a unique technical environment? Then this position as an Aviation Procurement Coordinator could be the perfect opportunity for you.

As an Aviation Procurement Coordinator, you ensure that the right parts are available at the right time for aircraft maintenance. You will be responsible for placing and following up on purchase orders, monitoring delivery schedules, and ensuring that all administrative processes are handled accurately. Thanks to your efforts, maintenance activities can be carried out according to plan.

You will work closely with buyers, suppliers, and technical colleagues on a daily basis. This will not only give you valuable insight into purchasing processes but also allow you to develop knowledge of aircraft maintenance and the international aviation industry. This role is ideal for someone with a solid foundation in purchasing who wants to further develop into a specialized procurement professional.

You will work closely with experienced Buyers, Senior Buyers, and maintenance technicians on a daily basis, giving you the opportunity to gain a broad understanding of both the organization and the industry.

We are looking for someone who is eager to learn, takes responsibility, and works with great attention to detail.

